<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) REDUCES GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) REDUCES GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will reduce gasoline prices by 2.50 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport diesel prices will be cut by 0.90 drachmas per litre, DEP said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments come after lower world gasoline prices, down by $9.4 per metric tonne, lower diesel prices, down by $2.6 per metric tonne, and a softer dollar/drachma exchange rate, down $0.8 drachmas per $, it said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
